A||||18||tgowens||Photos from the 16th Annual Fiero Festival||||1||
Z||000000||tgowens||07-30-2000||05:55 AM||||I have posted photos on my site from the 16th Annual FOCOA Fiero Festival held in Louisville, KY for those of you who did not have a chance to go................ <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||07-30-2000||07:30 AM||||Great pics Terry! You captured some of the most beautiful Fieros I've ever seen! EYE CANDY! I could've spent all day just walking around that hotel parking lot <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Thanks for sharing and it's reminding me to bring plenty of film to the Kick Hill Swap Meet next month!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||14
Z||000002||Oreif||07-30-2000||07:32 AM||||Very nice collection of pics! Thanks, I wasn't able to attend this year.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||Robert||07-30-2000||11:16 AM||||Great work Terry.....<P>  Did they plan to have the show under the freeway, or was that just to get out of the rain?  Did they have a trophy for longest distance traveled (and did you win)?  I think I like the “cop” Fiero the best, was it sponsored by a real police department?  Are these enough questions?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Later<BR>Robert<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">  <p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 07-30-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000004||tgowens||07-30-2000||01:44 PM||||Robert, no, yes, yes, no, no, yes.||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||07-30-2000||01:54 PM||||Robert, just messin' with ya! -- the plan was a parking lot show at the Ramada but the rain wouldn't let up so the County Go. allowed the use of the space under the I-65 bridge -- it kept most of us out of the rain but the ones on the ends kept getting wet. We did have a good time tho. <P>Yes they had a trophy for distance travelled and no I didn't win - they told me that a Fiero had travelled from San Diego and went 2,873 miles (which i can't understand since I have made that trip many times and I didn't go that far) but the route that i had to travel (going from Paso I had to go either up or down half the state just to get out of CA) I still believe was further -- oh well...........<P>the "cop" car was privately owned I do believe but it was a good entry. I have seen Fieros as Dare cars before (there is one in Cincinnati at the Delhi Police Department and I used to see that one daily) -- not sure where this one was from......<P>Glad you enjoyed the pics - with that many cars it was hard to really get close enough yet capture them all........I will tell you this -- I have never seen so many yellow GT's in my life!! -- HA! there were only two gold GT's, mine and an '86. That's ok, they do stand out in yellow (and besides, you have the cool scoops on the side!!!)<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||07-30-2000||01:56 PM||||Gokart, you should have been there (with Gokart'sGirl too!) -- there were people asking about you there as well as asking if Oreif was there -- we did miss you guys!!! Maybe next time, huh?||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||07-30-2000||06:35 PM||||Nice collection of photos, Terry.  It was great to finally meet you.||||reg||14
Z||000008||ChadMan||07-30-2000||07:31 PM||||I'll second that - great photos and it was great to meet you, Terry!  There was a med red metallic 88 GT in the show with Hawaii plates, but it must not have truly been a Hawaii car, because the trophy for "most miles covered to get to show" went to New York Joe (who, strangely enough, was from southern California).<P>I was parked right under a leaky spot in the bridge.  After wiping dirty water off my car 4x, I gave up and let it get filthy.  I don't think I would have won anything anyway - all us 4-cyl Coupes were in the same class this year and there were several there nicer than mine.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfixit58||07-30-2000||07:51 PM||||Terry,<P>Thanks for the pics. Looks like the rain didn't dampen the spirts of the participants. Who owned the blue GT behind you? It looks like the one I just bought.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||tgowens||07-30-2000||07:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR><B>Nice collection of photos, Terry.  It was great to finally meet you.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It was certainly great to meet you too and Drew WilliamThornIII and Boilermaker and Old Lar and EZsurf and 2M4Dale and Christine and Phil and Chad and I know I'm leaving somebody out....it is always nice to put faces with the names - that means a lot to me...<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||tgowens||07-30-2000||07:59 PM||||ChadMan, I felt a little cheated on that one since MapQuest lists the distance from San Diego to Jeffersonville at 2,114.7 miles and from Paso Robles to Jeffersonville at 2,213.8 miles -- if he took a 600 mile detour to visit somebody that is something else -- I coulda driven from Paso Robles to Virginia Beach and back to Jeffersonville and claimed that I guess - I'm not sure where they got their figures but I didn't think it was right at all.<P>It was good to meet you and we both had the fun of showing even though there were others there who may have exceed our car's quality -- it's good experience, it's fun, and it lets you know what to shot for next year -- good luck to you and stay in touch.||||reg||1
Z||000012||tgowens||07-30-2000||08:02 PM||||mrfixit58, The blue '87 behind me was owned by Barbara Mack, she bought it about a month ago for about $12,000 as it only has 4,401 miles on it and it goes to shows on a trailer and leaves on a trailer -- i think it a little unfair to compete in a Stock class with the "daily drivers" (like mine) when in that condition but, so be it.......it was a beautiful car - in fact, I voted for it......||||reg||1
Z||000013||Old Lar||07-30-2000||10:41 PM||||Barb Hack owned the Blue GT.  She should have entered a historical category with other trailered exceptionaly low milage Fieros.  One had only 1800 miles on it.  They are good reference cars so you can see how they were built.  But you can enter your car in either category.  Its hard to vote.  If all things are equal, the higher milage car should get the win.  But Barb's car was exceptional.  The third place car was the other Blue GT owned by the Prezzz.<P>Chris Moore did win peoples choice award with his Northstar GT.  Best of show went to a stock 88 red ttop GT with leather.  Frank Genova has won best 88 stock GT at FOCOA nationals for the last 6 years.  It is an exceptionally clean car that Frank does drive (in nice weather).  He had an 800 mile trip back to the NYC area on Sunday.||||reg||3
Z||000014||fiero56||07-31-2000||12:18 AM||||Hi tgowens,<P>Had a great time meeting you at the show. I even saw parts of my car in your pictures. Your GT is looking great, especially those wheels, I still can't decided what to do with mine now.<P>Those stock blue '87GTs looked VERY good. I have never been a fan of the fastbacks, but those blue ones, almost made me want to trade my Fiero for one(don't think they would take a 160K mile formula in trade though). If I ever buy a fastback, it will only be in that blue. VERY nice!<P>I also got meet 2M4 Dale and his wife. Very nice people, and a great looking coupe. He even took third place with it.<P>I also got to meet Phil(forum Phil, not Fiero-Phil) and see his beautifull s/c 3800 yellow Formula. Great looking engine, and even better looking car.  VERY nice guy. I have been eager to meet him for some time now. I saw his car in the lot at the hotel the night before the show, and couldn't wait to meet him.  I took a couple digital pics of his car, will post them tommorrow.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 07-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||fieroshop||07-31-2000||12:44 AM||||Terry, I'm leaving here on Thursday the 3rd of Aug. I will take a bunch of pics and will e-mail them to you. I think John Szpara is going up there as well. (That is if we get his car done on time.) He had another accident, as he was leaving to go his mother's funeral and they were leaving the shopping center, some clow decided that his nose was to far out on the street so he put his car in reverse and backed right into John's GT. That's the 3rd time to our body shop. Insurance pays again.||||reg||1
Z||000016||2M4 Dale||07-31-2000||10:15 AM||||Thanks, Terry for gettin' a pic of my coupe into your nice gallery.<BR>I was very nice meeting you. I thought it was really cool gettin' to meet a bunch of you guys at the show.<BR>I got to meet: tgowens,fiero56,Boilermaker,WilliamThornIII,<BR>EZE Surf,paul88gt,Rodney Dickman,and I know there were a couple of others. (I allready know 87ECO5 and ChadMan...lol) What a bunch of GREAT Guys !!!<P>Hey Boilermaker you need to get that pool cue warmed up a little more...lol <p>[This message has been edited by 2M4 Dale (edited 07-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||tgowens||07-31-2000||05:02 PM||||Thanks Dale - it was great meeting you and Christine too -- and I thought your car was a winner when I first saw it, nice to see that FOCOA thought so too!!||||reg||1
Z||000018||bHooper||07-31-2000||09:44 PM||||nice picks, Terry!  i wish i could've made it... maybe next year.<P>there were 2 GT's that had some extra ground efx on them, the red one (with black/white stripes) and the white/silver one. who is the source for that?  they look good on the cars.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
